<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Josef Terboven</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1898–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Josef Terboven was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">Nazi Party</a> official and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gauleiter">Gauleiter</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/essen">Essen</a> whom Hitler appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reichskommissar">Reich Commissioner</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> in April 1940. He held real power over the occupied country from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oslo">Oslo</a>, working with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidkun-quisling">Vidkun Quisling</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasjonal-samling">Nasjonal Samling</a> while repressing resistance through arrests and executions. He killed himself in May 1945 when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> surrendered.</p></div>
